{% comment %}
  Hemp — the farm hero.

  A locked-off golden-hour farm scene: a man standing with a horse, a dog, a cat
  and a hen, and a hemp leaf in the bottom-left foreground. Five thin rings of
  light glow around the five figures — green, blue, violet, amber, coral — which
  is the whole "for you, and for the ones who follow you" idea in one image,
  with **no copy baked into the plate**.

  The plate is a **still**, `assets/hemp-farm-plate.jpg`. Everything that moves is
  drawn over it, in SVG, in plate pixels: each ring starts flat on the grass and
  swings up and over its figure, then breathes. No frame is ever re-synthesised,
  so nothing can drift or wobble — which is exactly what killed the filmed
  version (see `docs/hero-film.md`, kept as the record of it).

  The SVG crops like the image does — `xMidYMid slice` against the plate's
  `object-fit: cover; object-position: center 50%` — so a ring lands on its
  subject at every viewport width, including the phone crop.

  The movement is in the type, not in the picture: the eyebrow, each line of the
  headline, the lede, the buttons and the footnote arrive one after another from
  the top down, each wiped in from its own top edge. Nothing pins, parallaxes or
  drifts, because the whole point of a still is that it cannot wobble.

  The rings are drawn as light — a gradient stroke that is pale where the sun is,
  a white specular segment near the top, a pool of the same colour on the grass —
  and they glow and pulse on three different cycles so five rings never pulse as
  one. On desktop three pills sit in the grass at the feet of the horse, the man
  and the dog: they are the hero's links to those three collections, and they are
  hidden under 900px, where the plate is cropped to its middle third.

  The plate is bright at the top and the leaf is dark at the lower left, so the
  scrim is a green-to-transparent band across the top for the headline, a softer
  band down the left over the leaf, and a fade at the foot that blends the plate
  into the ticker below. The rings are painted **above** the scrim, so they keep
  their colour where the headline's band is heaviest.

  `section.settings.video` replaces the whole thing with anything from Content →
  Files, if a film is ever wanted again. With a video set the rings are not drawn
  — the footage brings its own — and the pause control appears.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign poster_url = 'hemp-farm-poster.jpg' | asset_url
  if section.settings.poster != blank
    assign poster_url = section.settings.poster | image_url: width: 2400
  endif
  assign cta1_url = section.settings.cta1_link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url
  assign cta2_url = section.settings.cta2_link | default: routes.collections_url
-%}

<section class="hemp-hero hemp-hero--{{ section.settings.height }} full-width" data-hemp-hero>
  <div class="hemp-hero__media">
    {%- if section.settings.video != blank -%}
      <video
        class="hemp-hero__video"
        autoplay
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        poster="{{ poster_url }}"
        aria-hidden="true"
        tabindex="-1"
      >
        {%- for source in section.settings.video.sources -%}
          <source src="{{ source.url }}" type="{{ source.mime_type }}">
        {%- endfor -%}
      </video>
    {%- else -%}
      <img
        class="hemp-hero__plate"
        src="{{ 'hemp-farm-plate.jpg' | asset_url }}"
        srcset="{{ 'hemp-farm-plate-720.jpg' | asset_url }} 1280w, {{ 'hemp-farm-plate.jpg' | asset_url }} 1920w"
        sizes="100vw"
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        alt=""
        fetchpriority="high"
        decoding="async"
      >
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="hemp-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    {%- if section.settings.video == blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        One ring per figure, in plate pixels — the viewBox *is* the plate,
        1920 × 1080. The outer `<g>` moves the origin to the point where the ring
        touches the ground (`cx`, `cy + r`), so the circle's own `scaleY()` pivots
        there with no `transform-box` and no `transform-origin` involved at all.
        That is the one construct that has never varied between browsers — and
        the reason the first version of this came out lying flat on the grass.
        Radii were fitted to the five figures, not guessed.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <svg
        class="hemp-hero__rings"
        viewBox="0 0 1920 1080"
        preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"
        focusable="false"
      >
        <defs>
          <filter
            id="hemp-ring-bloom-{{ section.id }}"
            x="-40%"
            y="-40%"
            width="180%"
            height="180%"
          >
            <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="9"></feGaussianBlur>
          </filter>

          {%- comment -%}
            Four paints per figure: a linear gradient for the ring itself — pale
            where the sun is, saturated at the bottom, so it reads as light and
            not as a drawn circle — and a radial for the pool it throws on the
            grass. Literal colours rather than tokens, because an SVG paint
            server cannot inherit `currentColor`.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <linearGradient id="hemp-ring-line-horse" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f0ffcf"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#a6de54"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#a6de54" stop-opacity="0.5"></stop>
          </linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="hemp-ring-pool-horse">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#a6de54" stop-opacity="0.55"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.6" stop-color="#a6de54" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#a6de54" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
          </radialGradient>

          <linearGradient id="hemp-ring-line-man" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#e8f9ff"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#79c6ef"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#79c6ef" stop-opacity="0.5"></stop>
          </linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="hemp-ring-pool-man">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#79c6ef" stop-opacity="0.55"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.6" stop-color="#79c6ef" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#79c6ef" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
          </radialGradient>

          <linearGradient id="hemp-ring-line-dog" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#fff4d6"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#f2ba55"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#f2ba55" stop-opacity="0.5"></stop>
          </linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="hemp-ring-pool-dog">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f2ba55" stop-opacity="0.55"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.6" stop-color="#f2ba55" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#f2ba55" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
          </radialGradient>

          <linearGradient id="hemp-ring-line-hen" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#ffe6de"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#f08a72"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#f08a72" stop-opacity="0.5"></stop>
          </linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="hemp-ring-pool-hen">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f08a72" stop-opacity="0.55"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.6" stop-color="#f08a72" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#f08a72" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
          </radialGradient>

          <linearGradient id="hemp-ring-line-cat" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f4e8ff"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.55" stop-color="#b78fe8"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#b78fe8" stop-opacity="0.5"></stop>
          </linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="hemp-ring-pool-cat">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#b78fe8" stop-opacity="0.55"></stop>
            <stop offset="0.6" stop-color="#b78fe8" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#b78fe8" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
          </radialGradient>
        </defs>

        {%- comment -%}
          The rings themselves are decoration — the pills below carry the only
          meaning — so they stay out of the accessibility tree, while the SVG as a
          whole does not, because it now holds the hero's links.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <g aria-hidden="true">
        {%- comment -%} The cat, furthest back, on the fence post — hinge 1687, 524 {%- endcomment -%}
        <g class="hemp-ring--cat" transform="translate(1687 524)">
          <ellipse class="hemp-ring__pool" rx="120" ry="34" fill="url(#hemp-ring-pool-cat)"></ellipse>
          <g class="hemp-ring">
            <circle class="hemp-ring__bloom" cy="-114" r="114" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-cat)" filter="url(#hemp-ring-bloom-{{ section.id }})"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__line" cy="-114" r="114" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-cat)"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__spec" cy="-114" r="114" stroke-dasharray="214.9 716.3" stroke-dashoffset="-408.3"></circle>
          </g>
        </g>

        {%- comment -%} The man, centre — hinge 1130, 588 {%- endcomment -%}
        <g class="hemp-ring--man" transform="translate(1130 588)">
          <ellipse class="hemp-ring__pool" rx="137" ry="39" fill="url(#hemp-ring-pool-man)"></ellipse>
          <g class="hemp-ring">
            <circle class="hemp-ring__bloom" cy="-130" r="130" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-man)" filter="url(#hemp-ring-bloom-{{ section.id }})"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__line" cy="-130" r="130" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-man)"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__spec" cy="-130" r="130" stroke-dasharray="245 816.8" stroke-dashoffset="-465.6"></circle>
          </g>
        </g>

        {%- comment -%} The horse, left — hinge 760, 658 {%- endcomment -%}
        <g class="hemp-ring--horse" transform="translate(760 658)">
          <ellipse class="hemp-ring__pool" rx="137" ry="39" fill="url(#hemp-ring-pool-horse)"></ellipse>
          <g class="hemp-ring">
            <circle class="hemp-ring__bloom" cy="-130" r="130" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-horse)" filter="url(#hemp-ring-bloom-{{ section.id }})"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__line" cy="-130" r="130" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-horse)"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__spec" cy="-130" r="130" stroke-dasharray="245 816.8" stroke-dashoffset="-465.6"></circle>
          </g>
        </g>

        {%- comment -%} The dog, sitting — hinge 1360, 822 {%- endcomment -%}
        <g class="hemp-ring--dog" transform="translate(1360 822)">
          <ellipse class="hemp-ring__pool" rx="137" ry="39" fill="url(#hemp-ring-pool-dog)"></ellipse>
          <g class="hemp-ring">
            <circle class="hemp-ring__bloom" cy="-130" r="130" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-dog)" filter="url(#hemp-ring-bloom-{{ section.id }})"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__line" cy="-130" r="130" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-dog)"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__spec" cy="-130" r="130" stroke-dasharray="245 816.8" stroke-dashoffset="-465.6"></circle>
          </g>
        </g>

        {%- comment -%} The hen, nearest, at the viewer's feet — hinge 1592, 1048 {%- endcomment -%}
        <g class="hemp-ring--hen" transform="translate(1592 1048)">
          <ellipse class="hemp-ring__pool" rx="149" ry="43" fill="url(#hemp-ring-pool-hen)"></ellipse>
          <g class="hemp-ring">
            <circle class="hemp-ring__bloom" cy="-142" r="142" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-hen)" filter="url(#hemp-ring-bloom-{{ section.id }})"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__line" cy="-142" r="142" stroke="url(#hemp-ring-line-hen)"></circle>
            <circle class="hemp-ring__spec" cy="-142" r="142" stroke-dasharray="267.7 892.2" stroke-dashoffset="-508.6"></circle>
          </g>
        </g>

        </g>

        {%- if section.settings.show_pills -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The pills are the hero's real links to the three collections. They sit
            in the grass at each figure's feet and are drawn inside the same SVG as
            the rings, so they stay locked to their subject at every viewport width
            — only possible because the plate is a still. Positions are in plate
            pixels and deliberately below the copy column: a pill anywhere near the
            buttons or the shipping line ends up behind the type.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <g class="hemp-hero__pills">
            <a href="/collections/horses">
              <title>Hemp for horses</title>
              <g transform="translate(585 872)">
                <rect x="-75" y="-22" width="150" height="44" rx="22" fill="#0b2419" fill-opacity="0.82" stroke="#a6de54" stroke-opacity="0.55"></rect>
                <circle cx="-49" cy="0" r="6" fill="#a6de54"></circle>
                <text class="hemp-hero__pill" x="9" y="1" text-anchor="middle">Horses</text>
              </g>
            </a>

            <a href="/collections/personal-care">
              <title>Hemp for people</title>
              <g transform="translate(1040 706)">
                <rect x="-70" y="-22" width="140" height="44" rx="22" fill="#0b2419" fill-opacity="0.82" stroke="#79c6ef" stroke-opacity="0.55"></rect>
                <circle cx="-44" cy="0" r="6" fill="#79c6ef"></circle>
                <text class="hemp-hero__pill" x="9" y="1" text-anchor="middle">For you</text>
              </g>
            </a>

            <a href="/collections/all-pets">
              <title>Hemp for dogs, cats and other pets</title>
              <g transform="translate(1220 884)">
                <rect x="-200" y="-22" width="400" height="44" rx="22" fill="#0b2419" fill-opacity="0.82" stroke="#f2ba55" stroke-opacity="0.55"></rect>
                <circle cx="-174" cy="0" r="6" fill="#f2ba55"></circle>
                <text class="hemp-hero__pill" x="20" y="1" text-anchor="middle">Dogs, cats and other pets</text>
              </g>
            </a>
          </g>
        {%- endif -%}
      </svg>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="hemp-grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="hemp-hero__inner">
    <div class="hemp-hero__copy">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="hemp-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h1 class="hemp-display hemp-hero__title">
        <span class="hemp-hero__line">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</span>
        {%- if section.settings.heading_em != blank %} <span class="hemp-em hemp-hero__line">{{ section.settings.heading_em | escape }}</span>{% endif -%}
      </h1>

      {%- if section.settings.lede != blank -%}
        <p class="hemp-lede hemp-hero__lede">{{ section.settings.lede | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.cta1_label != blank or section.settings.cta2_label != blank -%}
        <div class="hemp-hero__actions">
          {%- if section.settings.cta1_label != blank -%}
            <a class="hemp-btn" href="{{ cta1_url }}">
              <span>{{ section.settings.cta1_label | escape }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.cta2_label != blank -%}
            <a class="hemp-btn hemp-btn--ghost" href="{{ cta2_url }}">
              <span>{{ section.settings.cta2_label | escape }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
        <p class="hemp-hero__note">{{ section.settings.note | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="hemp-hero__foot">
      {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}
        <p class="hemp-hero__footnote">{{ section.settings.footnote | escape }}</p>
      {%- else -%}
        <span></span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_toggle and section.settings.video != blank -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="hemp-hero__toggle"
          data-hemp-video-toggle
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          <span class="hemp-hero__toggle-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span data-hemp-video-label>{{ 'Pause film' }}</span>
        </button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (() => {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-hemp-hero]').forEach((hero) => {
      if (hero.dataset.init) return;
      hero.dataset.init = '1';

      const video = hero.querySelector('video');
      const toggle = hero.querySelector('[data-hemp-video-toggle]');

      // The rings are pure CSS and need no script. This is only a safety net: if
      // a ring is still lying flat long after it should have risen, something in
      // the browser has wedged the animation, and a ring standing still beats one
      // lying on the grass. Costs one timer, changes nothing in the normal case.
      const rings = hero.querySelectorAll('.hemp-ring');
      if (rings.length) {
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          rings.forEach((ring) => {
            const line = ring.querySelector('.hemp-ring__line');
            if (!line) return;
            let squash = 1;
            try {
              const t = window.getComputedStyle(line).transform;
              squash = t === 'none' ? 1 : new DOMMatrixReadOnly(t).d;
            } catch (error) {
              squash = 1;
            }
            if (Math.abs(squash) < 0.5) {
              ring.style.animation = 'none';
              ring.querySelectorAll('circle').forEach((circle) => {
                circle.style.animation = 'none';
              });
            }
          });
        }, 4000);
      }

      // Same net for the copy. `both` keeps a line invisible until its delay has
      // elapsed, so one wedged animation would hide the headline for good — and a
      // headline that arrives late beats one that never arrives at all.
      const copy = hero.querySelectorAll(
        '.hemp-eyebrow, .hemp-hero__line, .hemp-hero__lede, .hemp-hero__actions, .hemp-hero__note, .hemp-hero__footnote'
      );
      if (copy.length) {
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          copy.forEach((line) => {
            if (window.getComputedStyle(line).opacity < 0.5) {
              line.style.animation = 'none';
              line.style.clipPath = 'none';
            }
          });
        }, 4000);
      }

      if (!video) return;

      const label = toggle && toggle.querySelector('[data-hemp-video-label]');

      const setPaused = (paused) => {
        if (paused) {
          video.pause();
        } else {
          const played = video.play();
          if (played && played.catch) played.catch(() => {});
        }
        hero.dataset.paused = paused ? 'true' : 'false';
        if (toggle) toggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(paused));
        if (label) label.textContent = paused ? 'Play film' : 'Pause film';
      };

      // A poster is a perfectly good hero. Nobody asked for motion they did not want.
      if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) setPaused(true);

      toggle && toggle.addEventListener('click', () => setPaused(!video.paused));
    });
  })();
</script>


{% stylesheet %}
  .hemp-hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: var(--hemp-cream);
    background: var(--hemp-deep);
  }

  .hemp-hero--screen {
    min-height: 100svh;
  }

  .hemp-hero--tall {
    min-height: 88svh;
  }

  .hemp-hero--medium {
    min-height: 70svh;
  }

  .hemp-hero__media {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .hemp-hero__video,
  .hemp-hero__plate {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    /* The five figures run across the middle of the plate, and the leaf fills
       the lower left. Centring keeps the man and the dog in frame when a phone
       crops the sides away. */
    object-position: center 50%;
  }

  .hemp-hero__video {
    transform: scale(1.03);
  }

  /* ----------------------------------------------------------------- rings --
     Drawn, not filmed. Each circle sits in plate coordinates and is hinged on
     its own bottom edge, so one `scaleY` reproduces a hoop swinging up out of
     the grass: at 0 the ring is a line lying on the ground at the figure's feet,
     at 1 it is the circle around the figure. A single GPU transform per ring,
     no per-frame synthesis, and the last frame is the first frame. */
  .hemp-hero__rings {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* The rings are light, not a drawn circle: the stroke comes from a gradient
     that is pale where the sun is and saturated at the bottom, there is a white
     specular segment near the top, and a pool of the same colour on the grass.

     No `transform-box` and no `transform-origin`: the hinge is the origin of the
     circle's own coordinate system, because its parent `<g>` translated that
     origin down to the ground. `0 0` is also the initial value for an SVG
     element, so this holds even in a browser that ignores `transform-origin`. */
  .hemp-ring__line,
  .hemp-ring__bloom,
  .hemp-ring__spec {
    fill: none;
    transform-origin: 0 0;
  }

  .hemp-ring__line {
    stroke-width: 4.4;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .hemp-ring__bloom {
    stroke-width: 18;
    opacity: 0.34;
  }

  /* One bright segment of the same circle, up near the sun. */
  .hemp-ring__spec {
    stroke: #fff;
    stroke-width: 2.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  /* The pool of light the ring throws on the grass. It sits outside the scaling
     group, so it stays flat while the ring rises out of it. */
  .hemp-ring__pool {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* The pills are captions over the plate and the hero's only links. Desktop
     only: under 900px the plate is cropped to its middle third, and a caption
     with nothing beside it is just noise. */
  .hemp-hero__pill {
    fill: var(--hemp-cream);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .hemp-hero__pills a {
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .hemp-hero__pills rect {
    transition: fill-opacity 0.2s ease, stroke-opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  /* Hover and keyboard focus get the same treatment, since an outline on an SVG
     link is not reliable across browsers. */
  .hemp-hero__pills a:hover rect,
  .hemp-hero__pills a:focus rect,
  .hemp-hero__pills a:focus-visible rect {
    fill-opacity: 0.96;
    stroke-opacity: 1;
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .hemp-hero__pills {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* The delays run back to front — the cat on the post first, the hen at the
     viewer's feet last — so the field fills in depth rather than left to right. */
  .hemp-ring--cat {
    --delay: 0s;
  }

  .hemp-ring--man {
    --delay: 0.16s;
  }

  .hemp-ring--horse {
    --delay: 0.32s;
  }

  .hemp-ring--dog {
    --delay: 0.48s;
  }

  .hemp-ring--hen {
    --delay: 0.64s;
  }

  @keyframes hemp-ring-rise {
    0% {
      transform: scaleY(0.045);
    }
    58% {
      transform: scaleY(1.05);
    }
    74% {
      transform: scaleY(0.985);
    }
    100% {
      transform: scaleY(1);
    }
  }

  @keyframes hemp-ring-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  /* Standing, the rings breathe. Each element pulses on its own cycle — line,
     bloom and pool all different lengths — so five rings never pulse as one and
     the light never looks like a metronome. */
  @keyframes hemp-halo-line {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0.72;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  @keyframes hemp-halo-bloom {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0.2;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.52;
    }
  }

  @keyframes hemp-halo-pool {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0.45;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
  }

  /* Motion is the default; only an explicit "reduce" turns it off (below), so a
     browser that does not know the media feature still gets the movement.
     Longhands and literal values throughout, on purpose: a `var()` inside an
     `animation` shorthand makes the whole declaration invalid at computed-value
     time if that variable is missing — a silent failure that leaves the rings
     lying flat on the grass and nothing else to see. */
  .hemp-ring {
    animation-name: hemp-ring-in;
    animation-duration: 0.45s;
    animation-timing-function: linear;
    animation-delay: var(--delay, 0s);
    animation-fill-mode: backwards;
  }

  .hemp-ring__line,
  .hemp-ring__bloom {
    animation-name: hemp-ring-rise, hemp-halo-line;
    animation-duration: 1.4s, 7s;
    animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), ease-in-out;
    animation-delay: var(--delay, 0s), var(--delay, 0s);
    animation-fill-mode: backwards, none;
    animation-iteration-count: 1, infinite;
  }

  /* The bloom pulses on a longer, deeper cycle than its line. */
  .hemp-ring__bloom {
    animation-name: hemp-ring-rise, hemp-halo-bloom;
    animation-duration: 1.4s, 9.5s;
  }

  /* The specular rides the same rise as the ring it belongs to — otherwise it
     hangs in the air while the ring is still lying flat on the grass. */
  .hemp-ring__spec {
    animation-name: hemp-ring-rise;
    animation-duration: 1.4s;
    animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
    animation-delay: var(--delay, 0s);
    animation-fill-mode: backwards;
  }

  .hemp-ring__pool {
    animation-name: hemp-halo-pool;
    animation-duration: 8.5s;
    animation-timing-function: ease-in-out;
    animation-delay: var(--delay, 0s);
    animation-iteration-count: infinite;
  }

  /* The pills land last, once the light is on the five figures. */
  .hemp-hero__pills {
    animation-name: hemp-pill-in;
    animation-duration: 0.8s;
    animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
    animation-delay: 1.15s;
    animation-fill-mode: backwards;
  }

  @keyframes hemp-pill-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  /* Two jobs: make white type legible against a bright sky, and blend the bottom
     of the plate into the section below so the page reads as one surface. */
  .hemp-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      /* Top band: the sun haze the headline lives in. Kept heavy, because this
         plate is brighter at the top than the old film was. */
      linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        rgb(11 36 25 / 0.84) 0%,
        rgb(11 36 25 / 0.58) 26%,
        rgb(11 36 25 / 0.25) 52%,
        rgb(11 36 25 / 0) 68%
      ),
      /* Left band: keeps the headline off the lit edges of the leaf. Softer than
         it was — the leaf is already dark, so it does not need much help. */
        linear-gradient(
          90deg,
          rgb(11 36 25 / 0.45) 0%,
          rgb(11 36 25 / 0.18) 38%,
          rgb(11 36 25 / 0) 62%
        ),
      /* Bottom: blends the film into the section below. */
        linear-gradient(0deg, var(--hemp-deep) 0%, rgb(11 36 25 / 0) 34%),
      radial-gradient(120% 80% at 78% 6%, rgb(227 180 73 / 0.2), transparent 62%);
  }

  .hemp-hero__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    width: min(100% - 2 * var(--page-margin), var(--page-width));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: clamp(6rem, 13vh, 9.5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vh, 2.5rem);
  }

  .hemp-hero__copy {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .hemp-hero__title {
    margin-block: 0.35em 0;
  }

  .hemp-hero__lede {
    margin-block-start: 1.1rem;
    color: rgb(248 244 232 / 0.82);
  }

  .hemp-hero__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-block-start: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .hemp-hero__note {
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(248 244 232 / 0.78);
  }

  .hemp-hero__foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .hemp-hero__footnote {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(248 244 232 / 0.66);
  }

  .hemp-hero__toggle {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55em;
    padding: 0.55em 0.95em;
    border: 1px solid rgb(248 244 232 / 0.28);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgb(11 36 25 / 0.35);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    color: var(--hemp-cream);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .hemp-hero__toggle-dot {
    width: 0.5em;
    height: 0.5em;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--hemp-lime);
    animation: hemp-pulse 2.4s var(--hemp-ease) infinite;
  }

  .hemp-hero__toggle[aria-pressed='true'] .hemp-hero__toggle-dot {
    background: rgb(248 244 232 / 0.55);
    animation: none;
  }

  @keyframes hemp-pulse {
    0% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgb(216 242 107 / 0.55);
    }
    70% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5em rgb(216 242 107 / 0);
    }
    100% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgb(216 242 107 / 0);
    }
  }

  /* The copy arrives line by line, top to bottom — eyebrow, then each line of the
     headline, then the lede, the buttons, the note. Each line rises a little and
     is wiped in from its own top edge, so it reads as being "shot" onto the page
     rather than fading up as one block. */
  .hemp-hero__line {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .hemp-hero .hemp-eyebrow,
  .hemp-hero__line,
  .hemp-hero__lede,
  .hemp-hero__actions,
  .hemp-hero__note,
  .hemp-hero__footnote {
    animation-name: hemp-line-in;
    animation-duration: 0.85s;
    animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
    animation-fill-mode: both;
  }

  .hemp-hero .hemp-eyebrow {
    animation-delay: 0.12s;
  }

  .hemp-hero__line:first-child {
    animation-delay: 0.24s;
  }

  .hemp-hero__line + .hemp-hero__line {
    animation-delay: 0.38s;
  }

  .hemp-hero__lede {
    animation-delay: 0.54s;
  }

  .hemp-hero__actions {
    animation-delay: 0.68s;
  }

  .hemp-hero__note {
    animation-delay: 0.8s;
  }

  .hemp-hero__footnote {
    animation-delay: 0.95s;
  }

  @keyframes hemp-line-in {
    0% {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(0.5em);
      clip-path: inset(0 0 100% 0);
    }
    55% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    100% {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      /* Negative insets: the final state must not clip an italic's tail. */
      clip-path: inset(-8% -6% -8% -6%);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hemp-hero__toggle-dot,
    .hemp-ring,
    .hemp-ring__line,
    .hemp-ring__bloom,
    .hemp-ring__pool,
    .hemp-hero__pills,
    .hemp-hero .hemp-eyebrow,
    .hemp-hero__line,
    .hemp-hero__lede,
    .hemp-hero__actions,
    .hemp-hero__note,
    .hemp-hero__footnote {
      animation: none;
    }

    .hemp-hero__line,
    .hemp-hero__lede,
    .hemp-hero__actions,
    .hemp-hero__note,
    .hemp-hero__footnote {
      clip-path: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .hemp-hero {
      min-height: 92svh;
    }
    .hemp-hero__video {
      object-position: center 50%;
    }
    .hemp-hero__foot {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

